 "hook": {
  "text": "INDIA'S\nOLDEST GOD?",
  "until": 3.2,
  "y": 0.1,
  "size": 120,
  "accent": [
   "GOD?"
  ]
 },
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "This tiny seal may be ancient India's most argued-over object.",
   "emph": [
    "argued-over"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "In the middle, a figure sits on a low throne, wearing huge horns.",
   "emph": [
    "huge",
    "horns."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Around him: a tiger, an elephant, a rhino and a buffalo. Below, two deer.",
   "emph": []
  },
  {
   "text": "Archaeologist John Marshall named him Pashupati, Lord of the Animals... a name of Shiva.",
   "emph": [
    "pashupati,",
    "shiva."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Now look at the legs. Heels pressed together. Knees wide apart.",
   "emph": [
    "legs."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "A viewer of Part Five spotted it: Moola-bandhaasana. A yoga pose so hard, most people can't even get into it.",
   "emph": [
    "mulabandhasana."
   ],
   "caption": "A viewer of Part 5 spotted it: Mulabandhasana. A yoga pose so hard, most people can't even get into it."
  },
  {
   "text": "Scholar Thomas McEvilley thought the same.",
   "emph": [
    "same."
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "So is this the world's oldest yogi?",
   "emph": [
    "oldest",
    "yogi?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "Not so fast. Other experts say those are buffalo horns... and he may be a different god altogether.",
   "emph": [
    "buffalo"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "And the writing above his head? We still can't read it.",
   "emph": [
    "can't"
   ]
  },
  {
   "text": "But another Indus artist left someone we can almost meet... a girl smaller than your hand, hand on her hip.",
   "emph": [
    "girl"
   ]
  }
 ],
